Z||000000||Tina||01-07-2001||01:24 AM||||O.K.' here's the scoop.<BR>Found a blue 87 T-Top Coupe here locally in MN.<BR>4cyl, 5 speed, A/C<BR>According to him it was never driven in winter, but is stored outside( No Cover)<BR>What are my chances of it actually being rustfree?<BR>How rare are those, and options is it likley to have? Isuzu or getrag?<BR>And the almighty Q ! Is $2000 too much or a steal?<P>Desperatly needing help making up my mind<P>Tina||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||01-07-2001||01:43 AM||||That's a good find and a reasonable price, assuming it runs & drives nice and has no major defects.<P>FYI.....the 4-cyl Fiero came with an Isuzu built 5-sp......the Getrag was only available on V-6 Fieros starting in mid 1986.<P>||||reg||10
Z||000002||ray b||01-07-2001||02:27 AM|||| read the codes on top of wheel well drivers side in front trunk will list all opt.in 3 letter codes. blue is rare 87 only tops add value but can leak or rattle cond.+mls inportant to value if looks drives good take to shop lift check for rust.most shops will check car under 100. for genrial insp. ck compression to.        ray<P>=mls||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroMaster88||01-07-2001||02:40 AM||||Heck, go for it. What do u have to loose??||||reg||6
Z||000004||Old Lar||01-07-2001||07:55 AM||||T-top was not an option on an 87. The t-top code for an 88 is CJB and only 91 t-top coupes wer produced. It must be an aftermarket installation if the t-top is on a blue 87 (or repaintd 88).  If it was stored outside with no cover, and not driven in the winter, the paint would take a beating but the frame components should not suffer too much.  In the trunk area, pull back the carpeting on the sides to check for frame rust.  It seem to get eaten up in that areas easily. Price is hard to determine.  Milage? Maintenance of the car?  It is a 14 year old car, it may need some work. Find a shop that knows Fieros and have them look at it.  There are Fiero clubs in Minnesota.<P>I left mine outside for the first seven years with no cover throughout the winter (not driven in the winter).  I keep it really covered now, but still outside. I did have to do some paint touch up, still needs more.||||reg||3
Z||000005||Tina||01-07-2001||11:15 AM||||Guy is dead-set,that is an 87.<BR>I suppose they could be aftermarket.<BR>Actually,don't really care what condition engine is in. The V-8 would go in to it.<BR>My main concern is the condition of chassis.<BR>Did offer to bring the flat-bed to bring it to the shop.<BR>But the guy want's to wait till spring to sell it, could have something to do with all the snow here.<BR>So I can't get to the #'s inside either.<BR>Rather then undoing the rustdamage on my 84 and than beefing up frame, plus putting in the T-top of the 86 in,I though this would be much easier.<BR>Provided the guy is right about the " No Rust"<BR>So please<BR>Who has stored their fiero outside the past winters, put found that their chassis is still in very good condition?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||01-07-2001||12:16 PM||||ALL t-tops were aftermarket... GM didn't do the conversion themselves.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Archie||01-07-2001||06:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tina:<BR><B><BR>So please<BR>Who has stored their fiero outside the past winters, put found that their chassis is still in very good condition?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've stored quite a few cars outside over a period of time. I've noticed that cars that were stored on a "hard" surface (concrete asphalt etc.) Have held up real well. However, Cars that were stored on Grass or dirt just rusted to beat the band.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fformula88||01-07-2001||08:29 PM||||Give a good look underneath.  If its really rusty under there then its going to have rust elsewhere.  But if the bottom is relatively rust free (some minor surface rust is ok) then it should be in good shape.  <P>------------------<BR>John<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">    <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
